  "title": "Doubling CO2",
  "notes": "Concentration jumps from 280 to 560 ppm in 1850–1851. The dotted line is the equilibrium warming for that CO₂. Move the sensitivity slider: 1.1 K is what you get with no feedback at all; the textbook range is 2.5–4 K.",
